 <h3 class=3D"newsTitle grey_blue" style=3D"text-transform: uppercase;">Tra=
deStation: September 2026</h3></div>
 <p>In =E2=80=9CAdaptive SuperSmoother=E2=80=9D in this issue, John Ehlers =
presents an adaptive version of his SuperSmoother filter. The article descr=
ibes how the filter can be made adaptive while maintaining the improved fil=
tering characteristics of his original SuperSmoother, offering an alternati=
ve to EMA-based smoothing approaches. The EasyLanguage implementation plots=
 both the original and adaptive SuperSmoother filters for comparison and ca=
n be modified to plot the difference between the two if an oscillator is pr=
eferred.</p>
<p>A sample chart is shown in Figure 2.</p>
<div class=3D"figBorder">
<img src=3D"https://traders.com/Documentation/FEEDbk_docs/2026/09/images/TT=
-Tradestation.gif" alt=3D"Sample Chart" class=3D"shadow1" style=3D"width: 6=
10px;"><p class=3D"figCaption" style=3D"width: 550px;">FIGURE 2: TRADESTATI=
ON. This demonstrates a daily chart of the continuous emini S&amp;P 500 fut=
ures symbol, showing a portion of 2026 with both the original and adaptive =
SuperSmoother filters applied.</p></div>
<pre>Indicator: Adaptive SuperSmoother

{
	Adaptive SuperSmoother
	(C) 2025 John F. Ehlers
}

inputs:
	Period0( 20 );

variables:
	SS( 0 ),
	Period( 20 ),
	ROC1( 0 ),
	ROCRMS( 0 ),
	ROC( 0 );

SS =3D $SuperSmoother( Close, Period );
ROC1 =3D SS - SS[1];
ROCRMS =3D $RMS( ROC1, 81 );

if ROCRMS &lt;&gt; 0 then
	ROC =3D AbsValue( ROC1 / ROCRMS );

if ROC &gt; 2 then
	ROC =3D 2;

Period =3D Period0 * (1 - (0.5 * ROC)) * (1 - (0.5 * ROC));

if Period &lt; 2 then
	Period =3D 2;

Plot1( $SuperSmoother( Close, Period0 ) );
Plot2( SS );

Function: $RMS

{
	$RMS Function
	(C) 2025 John F. Ehlers
}

inputs:
	Price( numericseries ),
	Length( numericsimple );

variable:
	SumSq( 0 ),
	Count( 0 );

SumSq =3D 0;

for Count =3D 0 to Length - 1
begin
	SumSq =3D SumSq + Price[count]*Price[count];
end;

if SumSq &lt;&gt; 0 then=20
	$RMS =3D SquareRoot(SumSq / Length);
=20
Function: $SuperSmoother

{
	$SuperSmoother Function
	(C) 2025 John F. Ehlers
}
inputs:
	Price( numericseries ),
	Period( numericsimple );

variables:
	A0( 0 ),
	Q( 0 ),
	C1( 0 ),
	C2( 0 );
=09
Q =3D ExpValue( -1.414*3.14159 / Period );
C1 =3D 2 * Q * Cosine(1.414*180 / Period);
C2 =3D Q*Q;
A0 =3D (1 - c1 + c2) / 2;

if CurrentBar &gt;=3D 4 Then $SuperSmoother =3D A0*( Price +
 Price[1]) + C1 * $SuperSmoother[1] - C2 * $SuperSmoother[2];

if Currentbar &lt; 4 then=20
	$SuperSmoother =3D Price;
	</pre>
