ontract.</p>
<div class=3D"figBorder">
<img src=3D"https://traders.com/Documentation/FEEDbk_docs/2026/09/images/TT=
-Realtest.gif" alt=3D"Sample Chart" class=3D"shadow1" style=3D"width: 610px=
;"><p class=3D"figCaption" style=3D"width: 550px;">FIGURE 4: REALTEST. Here=
 you an example of both the SuperSmoother indicator and adaptive SuperSmoot=
her indicator plotted on a daily chart of the emini S&amp;P 500 continuous =
futures contract over about a year=E2=80=99s time. The adaptive period is p=
lotted in the top pane with a one-bar lag, showing the period in effect on =
each bar.</p></div>
<pre>Notes:
	John Ehlers "Adaptive SuperSmoother", TASC September 2026.

	Makes the SuperSmoother filter (RealTest built-in EhlersSS) adaptive by
	tuning its critical period each bar from the filter's own rate of
	change: ROC1 =3D SS - SS[1] is scaled by its 81-bar RMS into standard
	deviations and capped at 2, then Period =3D Period0 * (1 - ROC/2)^2 with
	a floor of 2 bars. High volatility shortens the period (faster filter);
	calm lengthens it back toward Period0.

	The period formula references SSadapt's own prior values directly
	inside the EhlersSS period argument: Ehlers filter period arguments are
	re-evaluated every bar and the recursion adapts statefully, as with
	AEMA. Requires RealTest 2.0.32.2 or later -- older builds run this
	script without error but compute a different, non-adaptive result.

	Plots the fixed-period and adaptive SuperSmoothers together; their
	difference is an oscillator whose cyclic turns align with the price
	turns and whose sign indicates the preferred side, traded here as a
	pro forma reversal system. The adaptive period is plotted in a top
	pane with a one-bar lag, showing the period in effect on each bar.

Import:
	DataSource:	Norgate
	IncludeList:	&amp;ES_CCB // back-adjusted E-mini S&amp;P continuous contra=
ct
	StartDate:	2008-01-01
	EndDate:	Latest
	SaveAs:	es.rtd

Settings:
	DataFile:	es.rtd
	BarSize:	Daily
	StartDate:	2009-01-01
	EndDate:	Latest

Parameters:
	Period0:	20 // nominal (unadapted) critical period

Data:
	// (1) Fixed-period SuperSmoother
	SSfixed:	EhlersSS(Close, Period0)

	// (2) Adaptive SuperSmoother: period fed back from its own output as of
	//     the prior bar. |ROC1| / RMS(ROC1, 81) in standard deviations,
	//     capped at 2; nonan holds the period at Period0 during RMS warmup.
	SSadapt:	EhlersSS(Close, Max(2, Period0 *
			(1 - 0.5 * nonan(Min(2, Abs(SSadapt[1] - SSadapt[2]) /
			Sqr(SumSQ(SSadapt[1] - SSadapt[2], 81) / 81)), 0)) ^ 2))

	// (3) The same tuning spelled out per the article's variable list, for
	//     the period subgraph; adPeriod is the period for the NEXT bar.
	ROC1:	SSadapt - SSadapt[1]
	ROCRMS:	Sqr(SumSQ(ROC1, 81) / 81)
	ROCsd:	nonan(Min(2, Abs(ROC1) / ROCRMS), 0) // ROC in standard deviations,=
 capped at 2
	adPeriod:	Max(2, Period0 * (1 - 0.5 * ROCsd) ^ 2)

	// (4) SuperSmoother oscillator: adaptive minus fixed
	Osc:	SSadapt - SSfixed

	// Pro forma signals: oscillator zero line (above =3D&gt; prefer long, bel=
ow =3D&gt; short)
	goLong:	Cross(Osc, 0)
	goShort:	Cross(0, Osc)

Charts:
	adPeriod:	adPeriod[1] {pane:ind1,color:darkgreen} // adaptive period for T=
HIS bar
	SSfixed:	SSfixed {color:red} // fixed-period SuperSmoother, overlaid on pr=
ice
	SSadapt:	SSadapt {color:blue} // adaptive SuperSmoother, overlaid on price
	Osc:	Osc {pane:volume,color:orange} // oscillator subgraph
	Zero:	0 {pane:volume,color:gray}

Strategy: SS_Long
	Side:	Long
	Quantity:	1
	EntrySetup:	goLong
	ExitRule:	goShort

Strategy: SS_Short
	Side:	Short
	Quantity:	1
	EntrySetup:	goShort
	ExitRule:	goLong
</pre>
