 <h3 class=3D"newsTitle grey_blue" style=3D"text-transform: uppercase;">Tra=
dingView: September 2026</h3></div>
 <p>The TradingView Pine Script code presented here implements the adaptive=
 SuperSmoother indicator introduced by John Ehlers in his article in this i=
ssue, =E2=80=9CAdaptive SuperSmoother.=E2=80=9D</p>
<pre>//  TASC Issue: September 2026
//     Article: Improved Filter Performance
//              Adaptive SuperSmoother.
//  Article By: John F. Ehlers
//    Language: TradingView's Pine Script=E2=84=A2 v6
// Provided By: PineCoders, for tradingview.com

//@version=3D6

TITLE =3D "TASC 2026.09 Adaptive SuperSmoother"
SHORTTITLE =3D "SS-Adaptive"

indicator(
    TITLE, SHORTTITLE, overlay =3D true)

//#region Inputs

int length =3D input.int(20, "Period")

//#endregion

//#region Functions

// @function Root Mean Square
RMS (float src, int period) =3D&gt;
    float s2 =3D math.sum(src*src, period)
    if s2 !=3D 0
        math.sqrt(s2/period)
    else
        0.0

// @function The SuperSmoother is a second-order infinite=20
// impulse response (IIR) filter, meaning that it uses two
// previous calculations of the filter output in the cur-
// rent calculation of the filter response.
// @param   src     Source series.
// @param   period  Critical period.
// @returns Smoothed series.
SuperSmoother (float src, int period) =3D&gt;
    float q =3D math.exp(-1.414*math.pi/period)
    float c1 =3D 2.0*q*math.cos(1.414*math.pi/period)
    float c2 =3D q*q
    float a0 =3D (1.0 - c1 + c2)/2
    float ss =3D src
    if bar_index &gt;=3D 4
        ss :=3D a0*(src + src[1]) +=20
              c1*ss[1] - c2*ss[2]
    ss

AdaptiveSuperSmoother (float src, int period) =3D&gt;
    float ss =3D SuperSmoother(src, period)
    float roc1 =3D ss - ss[1]
    float rocRMS =3D RMS(roc1, 81)
    float roc =3D 0.0
    if rocRMS !=3D 0
        roc :=3D math.abs(roc1/rocRMS)
    if roc &gt; 2.0
        roc :=3D 2.0
    int aPeriod =3D int(period*math.pow(1-0.5*roc ,2))
    if aPeriod &lt; 2
        aPeriod :=3D 2
    SuperSmoother(close, aPeriod)

//#endregion

//#region Calcs

ss =3D SuperSmoother(close, length)
ass =3D AdaptiveSuperSmoother(close, length)

//#endregion

//#region Plots

plot(ss, "SuperSmoother", color.red)
plot(ass, "Adaptive SuperSmoother", color.blue)

//#endregion
</pre>
